// "Cloak <card>" [CR#701.58a]: turn it face down; it becomes a 2/2 face-down
// creature card with ward {2}, no name, no subtypes and no mana cost. Put that
// card onto the battlefield face down. As manifest's, the face-down spec is
// the one `turnFaceDown` gives and the move's entry rider repeats [CR#708.2];
// turning it face up is the rules' special action [CR#701.58b,116.2b].
KeywordAction(
    name: "cloak",
    params: [Subject],
    spelling: "cloak <Param(0)>",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "cloak",
        frame_set: Transitive,
    ),
    body: sequentially([
        turnFaceDown(Param(0), faceDownWardedCreature),
        move(that(Card), wherever, battlefield, [FaceDown(faceDownWardedCreature)]),
    ]),
)
